\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Layer 4 drawn rather than argued. The released head asked for three objects emits three place points, $14.5$ and $13.0$\,cm from the basket. The basket is \emph  {not} fixed --- it is re-placed every episode, with a placement radius of $1.83$\,cm averaged over the suite's ten tasks --- so a memorised place point is wrong by $14$\,cm against a target that moves by under $2$, and $14$\,cm is enough to release a grocery over open table. \textbf  {Only radial distance is measured}: the angles are chosen for legibility and carry no information, which is why no coordinate grid is drawn.}}{13}{figure.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:placepoint}{{10}{13}{Layer 4 drawn rather than argued. The released head asked for three objects emits three place points, $14.5$ and $13.0$\,cm from the basket. The basket is \emph {not} fixed --- it is re-placed every episode, with a placement radius of $1.83$\,cm averaged over the suite's ten tasks --- so a memorised place point is wrong by $14$\,cm against a target that moves by under $2$, and $14$\,cm is enough to release a grocery over open table. \textbf {Only radial distance is measured}: the angles are chosen for legibility and carry no information, which is why no coordinate grid is drawn}{figure.caption.43}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {9.2}An instrument only ever shown firing is not yet an instrument}{13}{subsection.9.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces The positive control our detection-agreement instrument had never been given. ``Same-box'' is the fraction of frames on which two objects' prompt chains select the identical box; a high rate means the grounding stage carries no object identity. Run against \emph  {every} counterpart rather than only the ones that fire, the instrument separates cleanly --- and the split is interpretable: the chains that collide are the cans and bottles, the ones that separate are the boxes. Deployed binding is blind \emph  {within} a shape class, which is the regime LIBERO-Object's groceries occupy. Small $n$ (only $4$--$6$ of $60$ frames have both chains detecting) makes these demonstrations of discrimination, not calibrated rates.}}{13}{table.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:poscontrol}{{13}{13}{The positive control our detection-agreement instrument had never been given. ``Same-box'' is the fraction of frames on which two objects' prompt chains select the identical box; a high rate means the grounding stage carries no object identity. Run against \emph {every} counterpart rather than only the ones that fire, the instrument separates cleanly --- and the split is interpretable: the chains that collide are the cans and bottles, the ones that separate are the boxes. Deployed binding is blind \emph {within} a shape class, which is the regime LIBERO-Object's groceries occupy. Small $n$ (only $4$--$6$ of $60$ frames have both chains detecting) makes these demonstrations of discrimination, not calibrated rates}{table.caption.49}{}}
