\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Nine self-inflicted errors and their repairs. Every one was found by someone checking a choice rather than a computation, and every one ran in the direction that flattered us. The third is the one we would most expect others to hit: every check we ran had passed, and the defect was in \emph  {when} we looked. The harvester now reports each cell against its planned $n$ and refuses to report an incomplete one.}}{19}{table.caption.56}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:fooled}{{15}{19}{Nine self-inflicted errors and their repairs. Every one was found by someone checking a choice rather than a computation, and every one ran in the direction that flattered us. The third is the one we would most expect others to hit: every check we ran had passed, and the defect was in \emph {when} we looked. The harvester now reports each cell against its planned $n$ and refuses to report an incomplete one}{table.caption.56}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces What the two diagnostics require. The first two rows are arithmetic on shipped files and are what we would ask a benchmark to publish; the third needs an embodiment and is where our own result is weakest. The scripts are \texttt  {scripts/admissibility.py} and \texttt  {scripts/declared\_vs\_shipped.py}; both read a per-task table of object positions and are ${\sim }150$ lines. Porting them is a matter of writing the reader for another benchmark's state format, not of reimplementing the measurement.}}{19}{table.caption.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:portable}{{16}{19}{What the two diagnostics require. The first two rows are arithmetic on shipped files and are what we would ask a benchmark to publish; the third needs an embodiment and is where our own result is weakest. The scripts are \texttt {scripts/admissibility.py} and \texttt {scripts/declared\_vs\_shipped.py}; both read a per-task table of object positions and are ${\sim }150$ lines. Porting them is a matter of writing the reader for another benchmark's state format, not of reimplementing the measurement}{table.caption.61}{}}
